# tally 2.1.8 R13, the repaired definition (item 11 of the follow-up): n1 = days_between(a, b) over two windows is a
# computed value carrying both, a then b, so windows each takes a as each of its days and then b: nine lines (q5);
# the plain line is the print's hole (q4). big and big2 make 32 761 combinations, past S7's limit (q6). 2.1.8's first
# refcore dropped the carry at the def's read and left q5 the hole. The review's r13_two.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input a: date
input b: date
input big: date
input big2: date

def ab: bool
  rule base = add_days(a, 1) < b

def ba: bool
  rule base = b < add_days(a, 1)

def n1: int
  rule base = days_between(a, b)

def lim: int
  rule base = days_between(big, big2)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  a = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-03) "s"
  b = window(2026-03-02, 2026-03-04) "s"
  big = window(2026-01-01, 2026-06-30) "s"
  big2 = window(2026-01-01, 2026-06-30) "s"

ask q4: n1
ask q5: n1 windows each
ask q6: lim windows each
=== expect
q4: ?"date within window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-03) not precise enough for a print" (a)
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-01, b = 2026-03-02]: 1
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-01, b = 2026-03-03]: 2
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-01, b = 2026-03-04]: 3
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-02, b = 2026-03-02]: 0
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-02, b = 2026-03-03]: 1
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-02, b = 2026-03-04]: 2
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-03, b = 2026-03-02]: -1
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-03, b = 2026-03-03]: 0
  cut 2026-01-01
q5 [a = 2026-03-03, b = 2026-03-04]: 1
  cut 2026-01-01
q6: refused: RUN-LIMIT windows each over more than 20 000 day combinations
warning: WARN-UNREAD def ab is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def ba is read by nothing
